cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If PostureKit contributes to research or an assessment write-up, please cite it as below."
title: "PostureKit: evidence-first Windows, Active Directory and wireless security posture assessment"
type: software
version: "0.6"
date-released: "2026-10-17"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/abdullahzarshaid/posturekit"
url: "https://abdullahzarshaid.github.io/posturekit/"
authors:
  - family-names: "Bin Zarshaid"
    given-names: "Abdullah"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-8354-5177"
keywords:
  - security-assessment
  - windows-security
  - active-directory
  - wireless-security
  - evidence
  - powershell
  - python
abstract: "PostureKit reads a fixed set of security-relevant facts from authorized Windows hosts, records SHA-256 hashes for later integrity checks, and evaluates the facts against a transparent rule set. Importers fold in patch state, wireless configuration and network vulnerability scans. It identifies and evidences; it does not exploit, and severity is left to the analyst."
